On Jul 21, 2010, at 11:12 AM, Martin Kerr wrote:

> I'm going to need the detach/attach later on anyway and it's my main sticking point.
> 

Ok, I have added session support to the C++ client (it's a bit more legwork than what you have since you need to get both the port and the key and actually create a new connection to the session). The usage is roughly as follows (w/o error handling):

// assuming you have active, open Rconnection *c;

Rsession *session = c->detachedEval("x=rnorm(10)");
delete c; // close it, it's gone

// ok, do what you want ... just spend enough time for the eval to finish ;).

c = new Rconnection(session);
if (c->connect()) {
  // the session is not ready yet or something went wrong ...
}

// that's it = now you can talk to resumed session
Rdouble *x = (Rdouble*) rc->eval("x");
// ...


Cheers,
Simon

PS: I noticed that the C++ client actually has support for control commands - there is serverEval(), serverSource() and serverShutdown()



